<h2>Core technologies</h2>
<hr />
{# html, njk, vanilla js, css #}
<p>
  The basic "skeleton" of the pk-gov website, responsible for all the intuitive, informative and
  effective content you see here!
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    HTML,
    <a href='https://www.markdown-cheatsheet.com/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>Markdown</a>
    and
    <a href='https://mozilla.github.io/nunjucks/templating.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
      Nunjucks
    </a>
    are used to build the page content.
  </li>
  <li>CSS is used to style page elements.</li>
  <li>
    Vanilla JavaScript is used for dynamic page content such as services, no frameworks are used.
  </li>
</ul>
<h2>Development tools</h2>
<hr />
{# 11ty, vite, browser-image-compression, eslint and prettier, lottie-web #}
<h3>Static Site Generator and Plugins</h3>
<p>These are the tools we use to build pk-gov's pages from reusable templates.</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <a href='https://www.11ty.dev/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>11ty</a>
    is the Static Site Generator used by pk-gov.
  </li>
  <li>
    <a href='https://www.11ty.dev/docs/plugins/image/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
      eleventy-img
    </a>
    optimises images on pk-gov for a smoother viewing experience.
  </li>
  <li>
    <a href='https://www.11ty.dev/docs/plugins/id-attribute/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
      IdAttributePlugin
    </a>
    adds id's to all pk-gov headings to enable them to appear as search results.
  </li>
  <li>
    <a href='https://www.11ty.dev/docs/server-vite/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
      eleventy-plugin-vite
    </a>
    integrates
    <a href='https://vite.dev/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>Vite</a>
    into the build process for bundling and minifying code.
  </li>
  <li>
    <a href='https://www.11ty.dev/docs/plugins/rss/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
      eleventy-plugin-rss
    </a>
    automatically generates the Government news RSS feed.
  </li>
</ul>
<h3>Code linting and formatting</h3>
<p>
  These tools and standards ensure pk-gov code is consistent and easy to read for a smoother
  development process.
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <a href='https://eslint.org/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>ESLint</a>
    is used to check for errors in code.
  </li>
  <li>
    <a href='https://standardjs.com/rules.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
      JavaScript Standard Style
    </a>
    is the set of style rules used by pk-gov.
  </li>
  <li>
    <a href='https://prettier.io/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>Prettier</a>
    is used to ensure code is properly formatted according to pk-gov's style rules.
  </li>
</ul>
<h3>Other libraries</h3>
<p>
  From creating beautiful logo animations to compressing images, these libraries help take pk-gov to
  the next level.
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <a href='https://www.npmjs.com/package/lottie-web' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
      lottie-web
    </a>
    enables our ministry logo animations to play in their respective ministry pages.
  </li>
  <li>
    <a
      href='https://www.npmjs.com/package/browser-image-compression'
      target='_blank'
      rel='noreferrer'
    >browser-image-compression</a>
    compresses images that are uploaded to PIBSS.
  </li>
  <li>
    <a href='https://www.chartjs.org/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>Chart.js</a>
    generates informative charts and graphs for visualising PIBSS data.
  </li>
</ul>
<h2>APIs and services</h2>
<hr />
{# everything else #}
<p>
  These tools and APIs are as key parts of pk-gov services, helping to store PIBSS data, provide
  weather data and more.
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <a href='https://pagefind.app/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>Pagefind</a>
    provides pk-gov's search functionality.
  </li>
  <li>
    <a href='https://open-meteo.com/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>Open-Meteo</a>
    is the weather API that provides information for pk-gov's weather service.
  </li>
  <li>
    <a href='https://supabase.com/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>Supabase</a>
    is used to store and secure PIBSS data and images.
  </li>
  <li>
    <a href='https://mycal-web.pages.dev/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
      Malaysia Calendar API (MyCal)
    </a>
    provides public holiday information for the Timeline service.
  </li>
</ul>
